00:29:32.470 --> 00:29:34.870
For example, there's almost always a flow

00:29:34.870 --> 00:29:37.450
to handle when a user
forgets their password.

00:29:37.450 --> 00:29:40.750
Typically, what you do here is
ask the user for their email.

00:29:40.750 --> 00:29:42.850
You check that it exists in your system,

00:29:42.850 --> 00:29:45.010
and if it does, you send an email

00:29:45.010 --> 00:29:47.080
