00:29:49.480 --> 00:29:52.690
In your controller, you check
the submitted email address

00:29:52.690 --> 00:29:55.690
to verify and then you'd
craft an email message

00:29:55.690 --> 00:29:58.090
and send it using your library.

00:29:58.090 --> 00:29:59.200
It's pretty critical

00:29:59.200 --> 00:30:02.710
that this specific email
makes it to your user quickly.

00:30:02.710 --> 00:30:05.530
You don't want this email to
end up in the spam folder.

00:30:05.530 --> 00:30:06.700
They'll be expecting it,

00:30:06.700 --> 00:30:09.280
and if they don't get it,
they're probably going

00:30:09.280 --> 00:30:12.340
to quickly give up on whatever
it was that they were trying

00:30:12.340 --> 00:30:14.680
